{"duration_api_ms":43531,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fed1c8dc-6211-4efa-a88a-57e14156ea32","total_cost_usd":0.4029948000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":20,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30065,"cache_read_input_tokens":449774,"output_tokens":3622,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":798},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30065,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1615,"cache_read_input_tokens":52183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2719},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":3622,"cacheReadInputTokens":449774,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30065,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4029948000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":798,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":11,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"You were right to doubt it, but the problem isn’t the one you named. Q4 isn’t a count comparison, so the claim that “no species counts means it’s memory” doesn’t hold.\n\n**Q4: supporting sentences, printed from `sample200.json` (id `5a875fee5542996e4f3087ab`, comparison, hard)**\n\n- `[Lysiloma, 0]` Lysiloma is a genus of flowering plants in the legume family, Fabaceae.\n- `[Hydrocotyle umbellata, 0]` Hydrocotyle umbellata, is an aquatic plant that thrives in wet, sandy habitat.\n\nThe supporting facts are those two sentences only. I read every sentence of all 10 paragraphs too. Neither gold paragraph gives a species count; the Lysiloma paragraph is just that one sentence. So researcher read the supporting facts correctly. The conclusion drawn from them is where it goes wrong.\n\n**Why “no counts, so it’s memory” doesn’t follow**\n\n1. **The question compares taxonomic ranks, not numbers.** Lysiloma is a genus. Hydrocotyle umbellata is a two-part species name, a single species. A genus has at least one species, so “Lysiloma” follows from the word “genus” in the gold sentence plus the shape of the other name. That’s reading plus general knowledge of how taxonomy works, not recall of a fact about these plants. So I also disagree with your premise: this question doesn’t need both counts.\n2. **The context has even more evidence.** The distractor paragraph *Sabicu wood* [0] says “the wood of at least two species of the genus Lysiloma”, and *Lysiloma latisiliquum* is a second Lysiloma species. A model reading all 10 paragraphs has a clear signal: at least 2 against 1.\n3. **A correct answer here is weak evidence anyway.** It’s a choice between two names in the question, so guessing alone gets 50%.\n\n**What I’d change**\n\n- **Relabel Q4.** It’s a “rank inference” item, not a memorization probe. If you want to know whether a model uses memory here, compare its accuracy with no context, with the gold paragraphs only, and with all 10 paragraphs. One correct answer can’t tell those apart.\n- **Fix the filter researcher proposed next.** “Supporting facts don’t contain the answer” won’t find memorization questions:\n  - In comparison questions, the answer is one of the entity names, so it always appears in the gold titles.\n  - Yes/no answers never appear as text, so all 40-odd yes/no questions would be flagged automatically.\n\n  A better test: does the *deciding attribute* (a date, count or nationality) appear in the gold sentences? That check needs a person or a model judge, not string matching.\n\n**What I’m leaving open**\n\n- I haven’t checked how many other “which has more species” questions in the sample are genus-vs-species pairs like this one. That’s a known HotpotQA pattern, and those questions would all have the same issue.\n- I haven’t run anything with or without context, so I can’t say whether any model actually answers Q4 from memory.\n\nWant me to scan the 200 for that question pattern, or bring researcher back in to fix the filter?","ttft_ms":1701,"type":"result","duration_ms":169671,"uuid":"0d037311-64e5-4eb2-911b-715eb3b13580","ttft_stream_ms":879,"time_to_request_ms":361,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":9,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":26,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":1,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":0,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":290,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":2,"request_build":3},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":12,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":97,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"nested_memory","slowest_producer_ms":5,"cpu_ms":18,"major_faults":0},"first_content_frame_ms":879,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
